  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Saifansab Chandulal Tambolli vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 3 November, 2020 Ne In The High Court Of Andhra Pradesh At Amaravati \\ Tuesday, The Third Day Of November Two Thousand And Twenty :Present: The Honourable Smt Justice Lalitha Kanneganti Criminal Revision Case No: 392 Of 2020 Between: Saifansab Chandulal Tambolli, S/o Chandulal Tamboli, aged 32yrs, Taj Mohol District , Solapur Maharastra -413213. ...Petitioner/Owner/3\" party And 1. The State of Andhra Pradesh, through the Sho of Anakapalli Town P.S., Rep., by its Public Prosecutor High Court at Amaravathi. Md. Ghouse Khan, S/o Md Share khan Sk. Mohiddin, S/o Sk. !mam Sk. Mahboob Gabbar, S/o Sk.Ameerhafzua |. Kondalarao, S/o Suryanarayana S. Prasad, S/o suryanarayana No a F On Siva Sankara Sahoo, S/o Govindarao ( R-2 to R-7 are not necessary parties in the Revision , no relief is claimed against them.",
    "facts": ", this criminal revision case has been filed.",
    "arguments": "3, Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the revision petition filed an application under Section 457 of Cr.P.C for grant of interim custody of his Eicher Pro vehicle bearing Registration No.MH13 CU 6971 and the same was dismissed. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the said vehicle was seized on 13.12.2019 while he was carrying tobacco products and basing on the same, the crime was registered for the offences punishable under Sections 307, 353, 270, 273, 328 r/w 34 of IPC and Section 59 (1) of Food Safety And Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"FSS Act\"). He further submits except Section 307 of IPC, all other sections charged against the revision petitioner were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. In support of the same, learned counsel has placed before this Court the copies of orders in Crl.P.Nos.12 of 2020, 7799 of 2019 and 2820 of 2020. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the~vehicle is very much required to the iano seinem aHRORE crt petitioner and retaining the Same in the police station will not serve any purpose. He relied on the judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in General Insurance Council Vs. State of Andhra Pradesh! | wherein it was held thus:",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3, Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the revision petition filed an application under Section 457 of Cr.P.C for grant of interim custody of his Eicher Pro vehicle bearing Registration No.MH13 CU 6971 and the same was dismissed. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the said vehicle was seized on 13.12.2019 while he was carrying tobacco products and basing on the same, the crime was registered for the offences punishable under Sections 307, 353, 270, 273, 328 r/w 34 of IPC and Section 59 (1) of Food Safety And Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"FSS Act\"). He further submits except Section 307 of IPC, all other sections charged against the revision petitioner were [LEAKAGE_MASK]. In support of the same, learned counsel has placed before this Court the copies of orders in Crl.P.Nos.12 of 2020, 7799 of 2019 and 2820 of 2020. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the~vehicle is very much required to the iano seinem aHRORE crt petitioner and retaining the Same in the police station will not serve any purpose. He relied on the judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in General Insurance Council Vs. State of Andhra Pradesh! | wherein it was held thus:",
